# secrets
.env

# Ingestion intermediates only. These are regenerable with load.py and chunk.py,
# and are never read at query time. Comments are kept on their own lines: a rule
# carrying a trailing comment is legal but easy to misread, and this file is the
# only thing standing between your Groq key and a public repo.
data/raw/
data/logs/
data/chunks.jsonl
data/*_dump.txt

# The Chroma index is a build artifact, rebuilt by `python src/embed.py` from the
# committed data/docs/ pages. Tracking it buys nothing and guarantees churn:
# these are SQLite and HNSW binaries that change byte-for-byte whenever the
# collection is opened. data/docs/ IS tracked, since embed.py reads it at build
# time and the *.meta.json sidecars carry the corpus date shown in answer footers.
data/chroma/

# The ONNX weights fastembed downloads (86 MB of model.onnx). Kept inside the
# project rather than the OS temp dir on purpose: the build command and the
# runtime then share one copy, so a cold start does not re-download the model
# before it can answer. Still ignored - it is a download, not source.
data/models/

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# editors / os
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
